 "body": "### Motivation\n- Close #480's concrete Claim 17-2 calculation while accurately distinguishing the proved real-part estimates on the directly indexed subline law from the source complex estimates. The source is `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex`, Claims 17-1 through 17-3 and the combined-point lemma.\n\n### Description\n- Prove the concrete X-Z-X scalar estimate from its exact X marginal, expanded line-point consistency, the separate X mixture, and projective Cauchy-Schwarz. Preserve all three scalar theorem signatures and proof bodies.\n- Give each proved scalar estimate a separate auxiliary blueprint entry with its actual distribution, completed evaluations, real-part conclusion, and measurement hypotheses. Keep source-distribution transport, complex comparisons, and concrete paired-line consistency explicitly open.\n- Document the completed point constructor through field-valued commutation, a Z-X-Z sandwich POVM, orthonormalization on the original spaces, and triangle inequalities. Retain the source's binary-refinement route and its ancilla obligation separately.\n- Replace the unused duplicate placement module with an import of the canonical implementation so both paths can coexist. Correct the prefix, Parseval-column, fiber, and Z-only module descriptions.\n\n### Testing\n- Focused Claims, Points, and PlacementSupport build passed; both placement import orders elaborate. C1/C2/C3, the point/subline constructors, and placed measurements use only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`. Concrete paired-line consistency retains its recorded `sorryAx`.\n- Existing-parser comparison confirms every non-comment token of Claims.lean is unchanged. Source-header checks, blueprint rendering/synchronization, all 1661 declaration links, global completion-marker axiom checks, LaTeX and gap-note checks passed. The gap note compiles to PDF.\n- Normal hooks and checked publication remain enabled. A fresh independent review must exclude all 16 prior corrected-request authors plus repair author `01a082a2-e8d7-7ab3-a512-e4afeec3b820`; the earlier 12-author requests provide no evidence. Exact-head CI and review remain required.\n\n---\nCloses #480\n",
