 "body": "### Motivation\n- Restore the original product line-point consistency defect from the conditioned\n  law used before the pasting step in `lem:qld-xz-lines` (#490), at\n  `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:950-963`.\n- Retain the exact discarded probability mass without assuming its subsequent\n  numerical estimate or claiming the full pasting theorem.\n\n### Description\n- Specialize finite-conditioning restoration to `nondegenerateLinePastingDist`\n  using `Distribution.avgOver_map`. The bound retains both the retained-mass\n  multiplier and the discarded zero-direction mass; `Combining.Lines`\n  re-exports the leaf theorem.\n- Preserve the stacked restricted-mixture and nonnegative-average results,\n  opposite-register consistency positivity, and the restricted line-consistency\n  bound with universal constant `C = 4`. The factors `2m` and `4m^2` correspond\n  to the source passage at lines 1038-1061. Retain the existing reuse of placement,\n  operator-product, and product-average lemmas.\n- Refresh from main while preserving both merge parents and every staged input.\n  The three conflicts in `Points/Consistency.lean` retain the explicit\n  `DistanceCalculus.applyOperatorToState_mul` qualification and the incoming\n  paper-gap citation. Public assumptions and conclusions are unchanged.\n- Stack base: `issue-464-consistency-discarded-mass` (PR #467). Issue #490\n  remains blocked by open prerequisites #464 (PR #467) and #455 (PR #460);\n  both native dependency edges are retained.\n\n### Testing\n- Focused Lean checks for `Points/Consistency.lean` and the pasting-restoration\n  leaf, plus the `Combining.Points` and `Combining.Lines` module build.\n- Canonical pending-merge loss guard; all 3365 original stage-zero entries\n  verified unchanged before the incident-log append.\n- No proof holes or bypasses in the resolved file or restoration leaf;\n  the three existing `Lines.lean` proof holes remain.\n- Full `lake build` passed (9182 jobs) through canonical `warm-worktree.sh`\n  under the machine-wide build lock. All 616 pre-commit tests and integrity\n  audits passed; the canonical committed-merge loss guard also passed.\n- Validation subprocesses clear inherited `MIPSTARRE_JOB_CLASS` and\n  `MIPSTARRE_HARDNESS_REASON` so routing fixtures use their own inputs.\n- `checked-push.sh` passed every changed-file Lean check, integrity audit,\n  and declaration-sync check (all 1415 blueprint declarations resolved).\n  GitHub confirms refreshed head `5ff7dc43c9549f189a6e3cac96a6e215d30c01cc`.\n- Canonical `ci.sh 491` passed all eight gates; all nine `local-ci/*`\n  statuses are success on the refreshed head. Independent review belongs to\n  main; the prior head's approval is not claimed for this refresh.\n- The separate `blueprint_leanok_axioms.py --ci` audit passed: no proof-level\n  `\\leanok` declaration depends on `sorryAx`. Statement-level warnings and\n  advisory duplicate-helper reports remain existing proof-status limitations.\n\n---\nCloses #490\n",
